 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T05:15+08:00",
 "answer": "The air quality in Singapore is currently **Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy** due to haze conditions. \n\n* **PSI Forecast:** The National Environment Agency (NEA) has forecasted the 24-hour PSI levels to range between **150 and 230**. \n* **Regional Breakdown:** Readings across regions sit largely within the Unhealthy (101–200) to Very Unhealthy (201–300) ranges, with regions like the Central, West, and East experiencing higher concentration levels.\n\n### Health Advisories:\n* **Healthy Persons:** Should avoid prolonged or strenuous outdoor physical exertion. \n* **Elderly, Pregnant Women, and Children:** Should minimize outdoor activities. \n* **Persons with Chronic Lung/Heart Disease:** Should avoid outdoor activity altogether. \n\n*For real-time updates and region-specific 1-hour PM2.5 concentrations before heading outdoors, check the official [NEA Haze Microsite](https://www.haze.gov.sg) or the **myENV** app.*",
